From: Firmware Security Maintenance <security@local.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] bpf: invalidate rcu after last unlock

Backport the complete relevant verifier correction to the retained Raspberry Pi
Linux 6.18.55 API. The retained process_spin_lock uses regno instead of a reg argument. Extract the existing check_kfunc_call RCU invalidation loop into the missing helper, including STACK_SPILL and STACK_ITER and clearing PTR_MAYBE_NULL. Reuse it for explicit RCU unlock without changing existing bool lock state or error guards. The retained five-argument traversal macro is preserved.

CVE: CVE-2026-90317
Upstream-Status: Backport [https://git.kernel.org/linus/180c7000712db77063b3a26f4c97e7dd9038f449]
Upstream-Commit: 180c7000712db77063b3a26f4c97e7dd9038f449
Stable-Commit: 7ae71629357d0a6d0bdadb929c7b296d5b7e61c2
Stable-Patch-URL: https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7ae71629357d0a6d0bdadb929c7b296d5b7e61c2
Stable-Downloaded-Patch-SHA256: ae13c4dd2614710413bd581572b628ae3d66431dcb25ffcfa1ef0b76f06de4dc

